Now the refactor design for `action`:

```js
// ── Pure helpers extracted from action() (gh-926) ──

/**
 * Resolve the PR anchor and ticket key for this run (#687).
 * PR-anchored runs key off the input folder name `pr-<n>` (or jobParams.prNumber/pr);
 * ticket-anchored runs fall back to params.ticket.key.
 */
function parsePRAnchor(params, jp) {
    var folderKey = String(((params && params.inputFolderPath) || '').split('/').pop() || '');
    var anchorMatch = /^pr-(\d+)$/.exec(folderKey);
    var prAnchor = (anchorMatch ? parseInt(anchorMatch[1], 10) : null) ||
        (parseInt((jp && (jp.prNumber || jp.pr)) || '', 10) || null);
    var ticketKey = prAnchor ? ('pr-' + prAnchor) : params.ticket.key;
    return { prAnchor: prAnchor, ticketKey: ticketKey };
}
```

Careful with behavioural nuances:
- Original: `var jp = params.jobParams || params;` then `parseInt(jp.prNumber || jp.pr || '', 10) || null`.
- `const ticketKey = prAnchor ? ('pr-' + prAnchor) : params.ticket.key;` — if params.ticket is undefined this throws; preserve by keeping same access pattern (params.ticket.key evaluated only when !prAnchor). My helper keeps that exact order. Good.

- pr_info.md parsing:
```js
function parsePRInfoMarkdown(prInfo, prAnchor) {
    var info = {};
    if (!prInfo) return info;
    var numberMatch = prInfo.match(/\*\*PR #\*\*:\s*(\d+)/);
    var urlMatch = prInfo.match(/\*\*URL\*\*:\s*(https:\/\/[^\s]+)/);
    var branchMatch = prInfo.match(/\*\*Branch\*\*:\s*([^\s\n]+)/);
    if (numberMatch) info.prNumber = parseInt(numberMatch[1], 10);
    if (urlMatch) info.prUrl = urlMatch[1];
    if (branchMatch) info.prBranch = branchMatch[1];
    if (prAnchor) {
        var authorMatch = prInfo.match(/\*\*Author\*\*:\s*([^\s\n]+)/);
        if (authorMatch) info.prAuthor = authorMatch[1];
    }
    return info;
}
```
Note: the original only runs the author regex `if (prAnchor)`. And logs 'Found PR info input folder: #' + prNumber — where prNumber may be null if no match. The log line: `console.log('Found PR info input folder: #' + prNumber);` — that happens whenever `prInfo` is truthy, regardless of matches. I must preserve: log after applying parsed values (using the merged variables). Keep log in executor.

