content.thinking:
Confirmed: eval'd scripts have EMPTY URLs — they can't be attributed to js/postPRReviewComments.js. So a plain `eval`-based harness can NEVER produce per-file V8 coverage. The FIRST session must have done something different: modify how the module is loaded for measurement — e.g., the first-session harness probably rewrote the runner to use `vm.runInThisContext(code, {filename: 'js/postPRReviewComments.js'})` — V8 coverage then attributes the code to that filename!

In the first session (hidden record 64, 10k thinking) I likely patched loadModule to use vm.compileFunction/runInThisContext with the module path as filename, or read coverage differently. Actually — record [64] thinking was about measuring; record [66] gave "694 /tmp/crapwork/crap_before.txt" — a 694-line report, so it worked.

Cleanest approach now: patch the MEASUREMENT runner copy to load modules via vm.runInThisContext with a filename. loadModule currently does eval inside a function. Replace eval with:

```js
var vm = require('vm');
